+// G-buffer research prototype: the world pass of a remastered frame draws into
+// four colour attachments of the frame target. Only the remastered lit
+// programs declare outputs 1..3, and only opaque draws may write them (the
+// colour mask of attachments 1..3 follows the bound program and blend mode),
+// so blended decals, glass and particles leave the G-buffer of the surface
+// beneath them in place.
+void EngineGL33::BeginGbuffer()
+{
